# Math-env MDX

When editing notes under `content/docs`, follow `.cursor/skills/notes/syntax.md`. Do not write `<Prose>`, `<KindFilter>`, or `id`.

- Root children only: `Definition`, `Theorem`, `Lemma`, `Proposition`, `Corollary`, `Method`, `Example`, `Proof`, and `<Recall of="slug" />`. Do not nest them.
- Attributes are static strings. Slugs match `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$` and are unique site-wide.
- `slug` is required on Definition, Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, and Method.
- `of` = uses / instance / proves. `see` = sibling, contrast, or other formulation. Sparse. Comma-separated slugs, no empties.
- First `###` inside an env is the title. Omit it on `Proof`. `Proof` takes `of` the fact and has no `<Statement>`.
- `<Statement>` is the canonical claim (graph preview). Notes go outside it.
- `difficulty` only on `Example`: `routine`, `exam`, or `challenge`.
